{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1552336-new-advantage-pack-patron","id":1552336,"title":"New Advantage: Pack Patron","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-13T13:56:01-07:00","id":1552336,"title":"New Advantage: Pack Patron","content":"So in Moonlit Path, we finally get one of the staples of WtA; Non-tribal patron patrons for the PC pack.<br /> <br /> And I am, in all honesty, a bit shocked how long it took. As I said above, having a pack patron has been an important aspect of a PC pack.<br /> <br /> It does make one ponder, why was this advantage not used in the core?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T14:48:20-07:00","id":1552338,"title":"","content":"It's a bit more complicated. This is one of those things in Moonlit Path that made me just sigh.<br /> <br /> The problem is that Shattered Nation introduced a Pack Type system that's similar to the Coterie Types of V5. Problem is: The text in Shattered Nation mentions something called &quot;Guiding Spirit&quot; for the Pack aka Pack Patron Spirit... but it never mentions the Rite of Patronage from the W5 corebook. And that Rite from the W5 corebook only talks about using Tribal Patron Spirits. Meanwhile, Shattered Nation just suggested (pg. 18):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, Guiding Spirits at three dots or above may provide the pack with a minor version of a Favor and Ban for as long as the pact exists. The Favor is a one-die bonus to a single kind of test in the spirit\u2019s purview once per session. The Ban is a separate action related to the opposite of the spirit\u2019s purview that requires spending a Willpower point to perform it after invoking the Favor. For example, a flame spirit might grant a onedie bonus to withstanding moving through a burning environment but might require spending a Willpower point to put out any of those fires. </div> </div> </div>So you get to Moonlit Path and aside from offering options, there's a bit of clean-up going on here as well. Because it says about this new Advantage called Pack Patron (pg. 51):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To benefit from this Advantage, every member of the pack must invest one Advantage point. If using the Pack rules from Shattered Nation, this is a\u200b Pack Merit of one to five points. Each point in this Advantage provides the pack with an additional non\u2011tribe patron to choose from when performing the Rite of Patronage.\u200b </div> </div> </div>First of all, terrible mechanic. If everybody at the table agrees who their Pack Patron should be, just make one PC pay one dot and then you're done. What's the point of creating options when everybody agrees who to pick? I mean, is the idea that if you only pay for one dot the ST is gonna present the players with the one choice nobody wants...? That's ridiculous! Also, making the players pay for this Advantage AND the Rite of Patronage is ridiculous as well. <br /> <br /> And it still doesn't integrate with Shattered Nation's Pack Type system. The way it's phrased in Moonlit Path, it feels like they're not going to use Shattered Nation's Pack Type system as a standard. That's a terrible idea. I know I said in my review that 99% of the Pack Types in Shattered Nation were boring as hell (which they were) but I do think treating Pack Types as this &quot;optional rule&quot; only to let it grow moss in the Shattered Nation supplement is stupid. Pack Types are simply a mechanic that will bring W5 on par with V5. It's not some revolutionary aberration. It's a mechanic that copies what V5 has done! Both the H5 corebook and the W5 corebook were poorly designed follow-ups to the V5 corebook. Because of some stupid notion of &quot;less is more&quot; that led to neither the H5 corebook nor the W5 corebook having an equivalent for Coterie Type, we now have Pack Type mechanics in W5 spread across three books right now. Instead of settling it in the corebook and supplements offering more options, you got this mess of puzzle pieces instead. <br /> <br /> But then there's the rumors... What the rumors say is that the Pack Type system from Shattered Nation isn't something the people who worked on that book came up with for that supplement. Instead, it's stuff they pilfered from the draft of the Hunters Entertainment version of W5 that never got published. And then it makes sense why that text in Shattered Nation never acknowledged the obvious conflict with the Rite of Patronage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}